## Description

This week on ThursdAI: open source models are closing the gap on frontier labs FAST — and we had the researchers behind them live on the show.

We interviewed Lou from ZAI about GLM-5 (744B params, MIT license, lowest hallucination rate on Artificial Analysis) and Olive Song from Minimax about M-2.5 (80.2% on SWE-Bench Verified with only 10B active params). Both models approach Claude Opus 4.5-level performance at a fraction of the cost.

Then, mid-show, THREE pieces of breaking news dropped live:

Google released Gemini 3 Deep Think — 84% on ARC-AGI-2 (up from 68% by Opus 4.6 just one week prior)
OpenAI launched GPT 5.3 Codex Spark on Cerebras for blazing-fast real-time coding
ByteDance's Seedance 2 shattered video generation expectations with multi-shot consistency, physics, and stereo audio
Plus: XAI's SpaceX acquisition and co-founder departures, Matt Schumer's 74M-view viral article on the acceleration, the "agent psychosis" sleep problem, and more.

